iminal penalties, exclusion from participation in state and federal healthcare programs, or prohibitions or restrictions on our laboratory’s ability to provide or receive payment for our services. We believe that we are in material compliance with all statutory and regulatory requirements, but there is a risk that one or more government agencies could take a contrary position, or that a private party could file suit under the qui tam provisions of the federal False Claims Act or a similar state law. Such occurrences, regardless of their outcome, could damage our reputation and adversely affect important business relationships with third parties.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Increasing inflation could adversely affect our business, financial condition, results of operations or cash flows.","block":206,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-038330","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-01","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001410428","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1410428/000110465926038330/xwel-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/30dc12ca89fcd20572f91468a12e39029791d4e2ca1af3ce1de16aefe4d85a08.bin","sha256":"30dc12ca89fcd20572f91468a12e39029791d4e2ca1af3ce1de16aefe4d85a08"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":344},"materialEvents":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"4a115c98e94dd103052fee5abd8ff54147175745f8a3755000e76c6113cfc400","quote":"XWELL’s subsidiary Naples Wax, LLC, d/b/a Naples Wax Centers (“Naples Wax Center” or “Naples Wax”) which was acquired on September 12, 2023, for a purchase price of $1,624, operates a group of upscale hair removal locations with core products and service offerings from face and body waxing to a range of skincare and cosmetic products. The acquisition of Naples Wax Center is intended to enable us to move beyond our airport client base with a business that can be adapted to a larger wellness platform while also growing our retail footprint to serve our long-term financial goals.","context":"Naples Wax Center","section":"ITEM 1. BUSINESS","block":94,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-038330","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-04-01","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001410428","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1410428/000110465926038330/xwel-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/30dc12ca89fcd20572f91468a12e39029791d4e2ca1af3ce1de16aefe4d85a08.bin","sha256":"30dc12ca89fcd20572f91468a12e39029791d4e2ca1af3ce1de16aefe4d85a08"}},{"id":"99522cc4da37d38bd3dfa205690c862a80829fcabd6fb46848e2eb82c4392226","quote":"Our consolidated financial statements have been prepared on a going-concern basis. Historically, we have incurred operating losses and used cash in operating activities. As of December 31, 2025, we had cash and cash equivalents of approximately $2,716. Subsequent to year end, on February 24, 2026, we announced that we entered into a private placement of Series H Convertible Preferred Stock with accompanying warrants for expected gross proceeds of approximately $31,300 before fees and expenses. $9,000 of the proceeds was used to repurchase certain notes and redeem certain preferred stock and warrants, with the remainder available for working capital and general corporate purposes.","context":"Our consolidated financial statements have been prepared on a going concern basis; we must raise additional capital to fund our operations in order to continue as a going concern.","section":"●The Series H Certificate of Designations contains restrictive covenants and terms that may make it difficult to procure additional financing and that may affect our financial condition and results of operations.","block":170,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-038330","for